  "verdict": "All 8 effect-proof files are byte-identical in upstream tag v261 and the host 261.2 source, and no patch/postPatch/preConfigure touches them. The only core patch (postpone-d-bus-queue-dispatch) adds an early return in manager_dispatch_dbus_queue() while the API bus is connected but not yet set up: it delays PropertiesChanged/JobNew/JobRemoved signal emission and reload replies only; transaction construction, job merge/redundancy/GC, dependency atoms, job-mode parsing and StartUnit dispatch are unaffected. v261->261.2 core changes (ratelimit CLOCK_BOOTTIME, async API-bus GetId + subscription serialization, first-boot file, timer weekday warning, scope chown idempotence, sd-bus vtable cleanup, hashmap asserts) do not alter START transaction semantics. Operational effect on activation: a postponed JobRemoved can only delay synchronous systemctl start/daemon-reload replies, bounded by run() timeout=60s -> exception -> HOLD."
}
